to places like Cannes

236
00:10:35,268 --> 00:10:37,217
in the biggest party
season of the year

237
00:10:37,481 --> 00:10:39,311
where girls roam the streets topless.

238
00:10:40,062 --> 00:10:41,203
Maybe it's a missionary trip

239
00:10:41,284 --> 00:10:43,587
and they're there
to convince the girls to cover up.

240
00:10:43,749 --> 00:10:44,794
Maybe.

241
00:10:45,252 --> 00:10:46,571
- Oh, Jesus.
- What?

242
00:10:46,675 --> 00:10:49,213
I'm fine with the nuns.
It's this guy that scares me.

243
00:10:49,457 --> 00:10:51,244
No profiling, Turtle.
I don't believe it.

244
00:10:51,386 --> 00:10:53,622
Have you seen <i>24</i>?
'Cause I have.

245
00:10:56,273 --> 00:10:58,405
- All right, let's make a move.
- What kind of move?

246
00:10:58,973 --> 00:11:00,374
The same kind of move I made

247
00:11:00,415 --> 00:11:02,587
when I was terrified
of Pete Minetto in high school...

248
00:11:02,669 --> 00:11:04,072
we befriend him,
make him love us.

249
00:11:04,133 --> 00:11:06,787
That way when he seizes the plane
and starts executing people

250
00:11:07,639 --> 00:11:08,716
he let's us go free.

251
00:11:08,837 --> 00:11:10,274
I don't want to befriend him.

252
00:11:11,614 --> 00:11:13,502
Then I'm gonna feel
no guilt if I survive.

253
00:11:17,831 --> 00:11:19,476
Are these seats taken, my friend?

254
00:11:20,328 --> 00:11:21,405
Great.

255
00:11:23,618 --> 00:11:25,405
I'm Johnny.
This is Turtle.

256
00:11:25,864 --> 00:11:27,062
Oh, and this is Ari.

257
00:11:30,746 --> 00:11:31,985
Ari's fucked.

258
00:11:33,290 --> 00:11:35,016
I'm an actor.
What do you do?

259
00:11:35,467 --> 00:11:37,436
I'm fine.
I don't know what you're talking about.

260
00:11:37,518 --> 00:11:39,771
If you're fine, why are
you out shopping for cars?

261
00:11:39,981 --> 00:11:41,829
What does one thing
have to do with the other?

262
00:11:41,890 --> 00:11:44,448
I want a new car. What, I can't
have a new car if I want one?

263
00:11:44,528 --> 00:11:46,477
- It's my money also.
- You can have a new car.

264
00:11:46,538 --> 00:11:48,405
I'm saying you might want to go home

265
00:11:48,446 --> 00:11:50,903
because there are probably
beautiful flowers waiting for you.

266
00:11:50,964 --> 00:11:53,063
Why?
Are you feeling guilty about something?

267
00:11:53,287 --> 00:11:56,978
I'm not feeling guilty, baby. You're
happy. You're fine with not going.

268
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:58,439
And you're happy I'm not going.

269
00:11:59,515 --> 00:12:00,794
How much are the Mybachs?

270
00:12:01,037 --> 00:12:02,095
I'll call you back, Ari.

271
00:12:02,237 --> 00:12:04,511
<i>Please check the board for rescheduling.</i>

272
00:12:05,563 --> 00:12:06,639
FLIGHT CANCELED

273
00:12:06,700 --> 00:12:08,406
You gotta be shitting me.

274
00:12:11,410 --> 00:12:13,379
- Baby...
- This is not your baby.

275
00:12:13,501 --> 00:12:15,227
This is your
underappreciated assistant.

276
00:12:15,491 --> 00:12:17,745
- What do you want, Lloyd?
- I spoke to my therapist

277
00:12:17,963 --> 00:12:19,953
and he said I should not
hide what I'm feeling.

278
00:12:20,075 --> 00:12:23,242
I should express to you my hurt
and disappointment about not going.

279
00:12:23,364 --> 00:12:24,872
Well, now that you've
expressed that,

280
00:12:24,933 --> 00:12:27,776
let me express my frustration
that my flight has been canceled.

281
00:12:28,222 --> 00:12:31,326
Maybe this is karma.
Perhaps you should do something

282
00:12:31,407 --> 00:12:33,336
to turn it before something
really bad happens.

283
00:12:33,458 --> 00:12:35,087
Today, Lloyd?
Under code red?

284
00:12:35,554 --> 00:12:36,975
I'm sorry, Ari.
That was wrong.

285
00:12:37,178 --> 00:12:38,461
Yeah, it was.
Now listen,

286
00:12:38,603 --> 00:12:41,263
call my boy Kenny Dichter
over at Marquis Jets,

287
00:12:41,405 --> 00:12:43,618
see if me and the boys
can hop on a flight today.

288
00:12:43,801 --> 00:12:45,709
- You're gonna fly private?
- Just do it.

289
00:12:46,542 --> 00:12:50,176
Maybe in France we'll hit the
restaurant of your choice, on us.

290
00:12:50,338 --> 00:12:52,590
The flight's canceled.
Let's get the hell out of here.

291
00:12:52,753 --> 00:12:54,763
Really?
That's awesome.

292
00:12:56,326 --> 00:12:57,856
How do I get in touch with you?

293
00:12:58,729 --> 00:13:00,525
You don't.
If it's meant to be

294
00:13:00,769 --> 00:13:02,799
we'll run into each other.
Be well, my friend.

295
00:13:03,965 --> 00:13:05,935
That girl is wife material...

296
00:13:06,036 --> 00:13:08,425
wife, mother,
grow-old-together material.

297
00:13:08,527 --> 00:13:09,725
Too bad you have a girlfriend.

298
00:13:09,726 --> 00:13:11,674
Yeah. You did promise
you wouldn't hit on her.

299
00:13:11,877 --> 00:13:14,166
I'm talking in terms
of presence for the film.

300
00:13:14,450 --> 00:13:16,257
The sister has to have that thing

301
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:18,812
that you just adore at all
times in order for her to be able

302
00:13:18,873 --> 00:13:21,390
to get away with some of
the more vicious things that she does.

303
00:13:21,472 --> 00:13:23,597
Speaking of which,
you could have come to my defense

304
00:13:23,658 --> 00:13:25,678
just a little when she was
quizzing me back there.

305
00:13:25,719 --> 00:13:26,734
- Your defense?
- Yeah,

306
00:13:26,775 --> 00:13:28,199
she asked me pretty tough questions,

307
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:30,250
you're just sitting there
like you got no tongue.

308
00:13:30,311 --> 00:13:32,767
You were talking the whole time.
What did you want me to say?

309
00:13:32,828 --> 00:13:34,921
She looked at you a couple
of times for reassurance

310
00:13:34,941 --> 00:13:37,581
- and you didn't give her much.
- 'Cause it's an awkward position.

311
00:13:37,662 --> 00:13:39,591
I'm her manager but I'm
also a producer on this.

312
00:13:39,702 --> 00:13:41,653
It's a no-show-type job title anyway.

313
00:13:42,342 --> 00:13:43,873
I don't want to jam it down her throat.

314
00:13:43,893 --> 00:13:46,066
Plus, it doesn't really matter.
She's got the script,

315
00:13:46,127 --> 00:13:48,035
she loved Billy,
so what do you want me to say?

316
00:13:48,117 --> 00:13:49,491
You think she loved me, suit?

317
00:13:50,872 --> 00:13:53,406
- Hey, what's up, Turtle?
- <i>Yo, E, our flight's canceled.</i>

318
00:13:53,542 --> 00:13:55,581
- What?
- The whole airport's shut down.

319
00:13:55,844 --> 00:13:57,712
All right,
we'll meet you back at the house.

320
00:13:58,342 --> 00:14:00,686
L.A.X. is closed.
There's no flights leaving today.

321
00:14:01,335 --> 00:14:02,391
- Jesus.
- What?

322
00:14:03,085 --> 00:14:05,197
I couldn't bear
going without you, baby.

323
00:14:05,298 --> 00:14:07,775
I know they closed the airport.
It's all over the news,

324
00:14:07,877 --> 00:14:10,131
so stop making it
like it's some grand gesture.

325
00:14:10,212 --> 00:14:13,181
Baby, what did we learn about
being passive-aggressive in therapy?

326
00:14:13,364 --> 00:14:16,509
If you wanted to go you should
have not said "I don't want to go."

327
00:14:17,139 --> 00:14:18,788
I'm tired of feeling
like I'm not wanted.

328
00:14:18,849 --> 00:14:21,429
Baby, what are you talking about?
This is a one-time thing.

329
00:14:21,895 --> 00:14:23,398
You came home last night
and you said

330
00:14:23,438 --> 00:14:25,652
that the hotel had screwed us
out of a king-sized bed

331
00:14:25,692 --> 00:14:27,663
and would I
"really be comfortable in a single?"

332
00:14:27,724 --> 00:14:29,541
<i>and then this morning
before the news came on</i>

333
00:14:29,581 --> 00:14:31,368
<i>you said that Brian Sher's wife
wasn't going</i>

334
00:14:31,449 --> 00:14:33,816
and if she found out
that I was going, she would go crazy.

335
00:14:33,918 --> 00:14:36,914
There are some men that would kill to go
to the south of France with me

336
00:14:36,975 --> 00:14:38,274
<i>and if you're not one of them...</i>

337
00:14:38,335 --> 00:14:41,217
I am one of them, honey.
I'm glad that the flight was canceled,

338
00:14:41,359 --> 00:14:43,552
so now I can tell you I want you to go.

339
00:14:43,937 --> 00:14:45,620
<i>I don't want to go without you</i>

340
00:14:45,863 --> 00:14:48,503
and I love you.
Now will you go?

341
00:14:48,847 --> 00:14:49,896
No, Ari, I won't.

342
00:14:50,254 --> 00:14:51,269
Why not?

343
00:14:51,451 --> 00:14:53,726
Well, because all that will
do is assuage your guilt.

344
00:14:54,691 --> 00:14:55,907
Why would you want to do that?

345
00:14:56,028 --> 00:14:58,848
- Well, you shouldn't feel guilty.
- What should I feel?

346
00:14:59,092 --> 00:15:00,574
Sadness that for some reason

347
00:15:00,655 --> 00:15:02,880
you're married to someone
you don't like to be with.

348
00:15:03,042 --> 00:15:05,940
Laura, I'll definitely
need some help upstairs.

349
00:15:07,048 --> 00:15:08,124
Hello, Lloyd.

350
00:15:09,009 --> 00:15:10,742
- Hello, Ari.
- You're not my mistress.

351
00:15:10,844 --> 00:15:12,636
Stop being mad at me.
- I'm no longer mad.

352
00:15:12,737 --> 00:15:15,011
You shouldn't be,
'cause I'd love to have you in Cannes.

353
00:15:15,052 --> 00:15:17,822
So go home, pack your favorite sarong
and consider yourself invited.

354
00:15:17,903 --> 00:15:19,742
- Are you serious?
- I'm so serious

355
00:15:19,924 --> 00:15:21,650
that I'm actually
embarrassed for myself.

356
00:15:21,731 --> 00:15:23,395
- That's very sweet of you.
- It's not,

357
00:15:23,436 --> 00:15:26,156
'cause I don't want to see you when
I'm there. This is a man's trip,

358
00:15:26,224 --> 00:15:28,234
so you're gonna have to
find your own dick clique.

359
00:15:28,315 --> 00:15:30,060
That is fine, Ari.
Oh my god.

360
00:15:30,487 --> 00:15:33,492
I'm so happy.
But how are we getting there?

361
00:15:33,695 --> 00:15:36,125
- You called Kenny D., right?
- He says there are no jets.

362
00:15:36,369 --> 00:15:39,252
The whole town is scrambling since
the alert and you scrambled too late.

363
00:15:39,374 --> 00:15:41,833
- There's not one more plane?
- There was one,

364
00:15:41,934 --> 00:15:43,505
but Sydney Pollack just booked it.

365
00:15:43,769 --> 00:15:44,906
Fuck!

366
00:15:45,271 --> 00:15:46,977
The airline said
that they can't guarantee

367
00:15:47,058 --> 00:15:49,247
that we can get on a flight tomorrow?
This is unreal.

368
00:15:49,328 --> 00:15:52,252
My travel lady says
we could drive to Phoenix,

369
00:15:52,333 --> 00:15:55,110
get on a flight to st. Louis and
then hop on a flight to France.

370
00:15:56,044 --> 00:15:57,791
- Sounds miserable.
- Beyond miserable.

371
00:15:57,912 --> 00:16:00,260
This is insane.
<i>Medellin</i> premieres in 48 hours.

372
00:16:00,362 --> 00:16:01,958
- We may not make it.
- We'll make it.

373
00:16:02,019 --> 00:16:03,786
Ari will take care of it, I'm sure.

374
00:16:04,517 --> 00:16:05,717
Hey, what's up, Anna?

375
00:16:05,818 --> 00:16:08,203
I thought you'd be on a plane.
I was gonna leave a message.

376
00:16:08,285 --> 00:16:10,173
No, everything got canceled.
Turn on the news.

377
00:16:10,274 --> 00:16:12,102
Oh, I'm sorry.
That sucks.

378
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:13,442
What's going on?

379
00:16:13,869 --> 00:16:15,168
It's about Billy's script.

380
00:16:17,635 --> 00:16:18,752
Can I speak freely?

381
00:16:18,854 --> 00:16:20,336
Of course.
What's going on?

382
00:16:21,209 --> 00:16:22,468
I don't get it.

383
00:16:25,010 --> 00:16:27,783
It's Sydney Pollack returning.
My fingers are all crossed.

384
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,933
Is this my dear old friend Sydney?

385
00:16:31,156 --> 00:16:33,522
I told you when I fired you
we weren't friends.

386
00:16:33,643 --> 00:16:36,766
You consider that a firing?
I like to look back at it

387
00:16:36,827 --> 00:16:38,939
as an amicable parting of the ways.

388
00:16:39,060 --> 00:16:41,665
I'm not coming back, okay?
You understand the word "never"?

389
00:16:41,848 --> 00:16:43,371
Well, you just keep thinking about it

390
00:16:43,432 --> 00:16:45,731
because this is not a business
call, this is personal.

391
00:16:45,995 --> 00:16:47,188
I need a lift to Cannes.

392
00:16:47,574 --> 00:16:49,462
<i>I heard you got the last plane
out of marquis</i>

393
00:16:49,543 --> 00:16:53,076
and I've got to get Vinnie Chase and
the <i>Medellin</i> crew there by tomorrow.

394
00:16:53,401 --> 00:16:55,965
<i>Medellin</i>... You know,
I hear a lot of hype about that film.

395
00:16:56,087 --> 00:16:57,874
It's phenomenal.
It's absolutely phenomenal.

396
00:16:57,993 --> 00:17:00,653
I'm not completely sold
on that kid of yours yet.

397
00:17:00,836 --> 00:17:04,160
After a plane ride and a screening
you'll see him as the next Redford.

398
00:17:04,424 --> 00:17:06,475
You want to do a
<i>Three Days of the Condor</i> sequel?

399
00:17:06,596 --> 00:17:07,713
No.

400
00:17:08,342 --> 00:17:09,784
I wouldn't mind reading him, though.

401
00:17:09,839 --> 00:17:12,398
You know, maybe something
would come up.

402
00:17:13,677 --> 00:17:15,667
<i>Okay, Ari, I'll give you a lift,</i>

403
00:17:15,990 --> 00:17:17,614
as long as I don't sit next to you.

404
00:17:17,678 --> 00:17:18,947
I'll ride in the bathroom.

405
00:17:19,495 --> 00:17:21,576
- <i>How many you got?</i>
- Six.

406
00:17:21,836 --> 00:17:25,532
I can't take six. I can do maybe five,
and that's gonna be tight.

407
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:28,597
We'll make do. Listen,
I still love you, Sydney.

408
00:17:28,770 --> 00:17:31,308
6:30 sharp at Van Nuys.
Goodbye, Ari.

409
00:17:34,333 --> 00:17:35,646
Come on.
It was a numbers thing.

410
00:17:35,707 --> 00:17:37,494
You heard...
I couldn't have done anything.

411
00:17:37,575 --> 00:17:39,199
- Where are you doing?
- To unpack.

412
00:17:39,443 --> 00:17:41,664
Unpack?
You couldn't have even packed yet.

413
00:17:42,131 --> 00:17:45,278
In my mind, I did, Ari.
Iin my mind, I did.

414
00:17:45,822 --> 00:17:47,284
It's not my fault she doesn't get it.

415
00:17:47,345 --> 00:17:49,518
But it is your fault
if you don't try and help her to.

416
00:17:49,579 --> 00:17:52,395
- What do you want me to say?
- I want you to say that you're gonna go

417
00:17:52,436 --> 00:17:54,131
convince her
that she should do the movie,

418
00:17:54,212 --> 00:17:57,415
because that's what your director wants,
and as a producer, that is your job.

419
00:17:57,699 --> 00:17:58,703
It's your job, E.

420
00:17:58,825 --> 00:18:00,715
How would you like me
to try to convince her?

421
00:18:00,959 --> 00:18:02,765
Tell her how great
you think it's gonna be.

422
00:18:02,843 --> 00:18:04,021
That's what she wants to hear.

423
00:18:04,082 --> 00:18:05,812
What if I don't think
it's gonna be great?

424
00:18:05,893 --> 00:18:08,308
Should I lie to her?
'Cause that's not what a manager does.

425
00:18:08,511 --> 00:18:09,689
You lied to me.

426
00:18:10,670 --> 00:18:12,994
What, you don't think I know
you don't like it?

427
00:18:13,075 --> 00:18:14,968
I don't know,
you've never asked for my opinion

428
00:18:15,008 --> 00:18:17,485
- before you agreed to do the movie.
- Because you hate Billy.

429
00:18:17,546 --> 00:18:20,221
I knew there was no way you
were gonna read it with an open mind.

430
00:18:20,262 --> 00:18:21,541
What, you're a mind-reader now?

431
00:18:21,582 --> 00:18:23,423
You asked me if I thought it was okay

432
00:18:23,463 --> 00:18:26,021
if you sign Anna as a client
and I said one thing:

433
00:18:26,203 --> 00:18:28,297
"just make sure
it doesn't affect my career."

434
00:18:28,621 --> 00:18:29,880
This is the movie I'm making

435
00:18:29,945 --> 00:18:31,671
and this is who
I want to be in the movie.

436
00:18:31,712 --> 00:18:33,641
And I really believe
it's gonna be a great movie

437
00:18:33,681 --> 00:18:34,899
and she's gonna be great in it.

438
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:37,056
You have to believe that
and try to make this happen.

439
00:18:37,096 --> 00:18:38,159
And if I can't?

440
00:18:38,193 --> 00:18:40,028
At least
make me believe that you tried.

441
00:18:40,521 --> 00:18:43,323
Hey, Ari called. He said we have
to be at the airport in three hours.

442
00:18:43,445 --> 00:18:44,462
How are we getting there?

443
00:18:44,482 --> 00:18:46,422
Sydney Pollack's
giving us a lift on his G-IV.

444
00:18:48,575 --> 00:18:49,732
Sweet.

445
00:18:49,871 --> 00:18:51,374
I told you it was gonna work out.

446
00:18:52,003 --> 00:18:53,221
It always does, right?

447
00:18:53,424 --> 00:18:55,752
- So do you really like the script?
- You really hate it?

448
00:18:56,138 --> 00:18:58,676
No, I don't hate it.
I'm unsure.

449
00:18:59,082 --> 00:19:00,515
You know, it's confusing.

450
00:19:00,962 --> 00:19:02,769
I'm really looking
for some guidance here.

451
00:19:03,121 --> 00:19:05,253
Yeah, well, maybe you
should give it another read.

452
00:19:07,446 --> 00:19:09,582
"Leopold furiously cooks breakfast.

453
00:19:09,846 --> 00:19:12,445
Curtis enters and Leopold,
overcome by his presence,

454
00:19:12,627 --> 00:19:14,822
sears his hand
over the hot sizzling bacon.

455
00:19:15,127 --> 00:19:16,507
Curtis begins to weep."

456
00:19:17,746 --> 00:19:19,739
- It's written in haiku.
- The guy's an original.

457
00:19:20,615 --> 00:19:22,706
I'm a little surprised
we're off on this.

458
00:19:23,072 --> 00:19:24,867
Maybe it's just
my head space right now.

459
00:19:25,070 --> 00:19:26,918
But if you think I should do it...

460
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:29,337
do you think I should do it?
I really trust your opinion.

461
00:19:30,576 --> 00:19:32,281
I think Billy's gonna
make a great movie.

462
00:19:32,342 --> 00:19:34,339
So you were happy
with what he did on <i>Medellin</i>?

463
00:19:35,618 --> 00:19:36,917
It got into Cannes.

464
00:19:39,407 --> 00:19:40,971
Okay, I'll do it.

465
00:19:43,722 --> 00:19:45,813
I'm sure Billy and Vince
will be happy to hear that.

466
00:19:45,895 --> 00:19:47,317
So do you have to go to the airport?

467
00:19:47,459 --> 00:19:48,962
Yeah, the flight leaves at 6:30.

468
